# ServiceLog — environment variables
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#   cp .env.example .env     (PowerShell: Copy-Item .env.example .env)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gemini API — server-side only. Read exclusively in lib/gemma.ts (Batch C).
# NEVER prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that would expose it to the browser.
# Create a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Open-weight Gemma model served by the Gemini API.
# Default: Gemma 4 26B-A4B (MoE, ~4B active params — fast on shared free-tier capacity).
# Override to try e.g. gemma-4-31b-it without touching any code.
GEMMA_MODEL=gemma-4-26b-a4b-it

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database — SQLite for local development (PLAN.md §10).
# Read by prisma.config.ts (Prisma CLI) and lib/db.ts (runtime).
# The path is relative to the project root. Changing the schema.prisma
# `provider` to postgresql and swapping this URL is all PLAN.md §10 requires
# to move to a managed database.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"